  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Song for Black Sabbath's Second North American Tour** (1 other source): Listed as an unreleased song, with no album attached [1]\n- **Soft Targets** (1 other source): Listed as coming from Bedside Recordings Vol. 1.2 [1]\n- **Lakeside View Apartment Suites** (1 other source): The notes list it as being from the album Transcendental Youth [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Intro (Agnostic Front - Victim in Pain)**: rare: 14 archived performances [5]\n- **Song for Black Sabbath's Second North American Tour**: rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2018-09-14** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 23 songs; 92 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **tmg2018-09-14.mk4.flac24**: source not stated; 22 songs; 92 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer says this is the only recording of a live-only song with Matt adding a sax line [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2018-09-14**: taped by LMGBTapes; transferred by LMGBTapes; source: SBD > Zoom H4n Pro + CA-14 Omnis > CA Ugly Battery Box > Zoom H4n Pro [1]. Also: The matrix recording is credited to Kyle, whose taping the reviewer follows [3]\n- **tmg2018-09-14.mk4.flac24**: taped by Lance Stack; transferred by Lance Stack; source: Schoeps MK4's > Vark KCY > Naiant Littlebox > Sony PCM-M10 @ 24/48 > SDHC [2]",
